       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for ibuprofen in adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under prescriber supervision.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks at this dose:** The main risks are GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove them.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common anti-inflammatory dose.\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours as needed**, a typical analgesic dose.\n- **1600 mg per day in total**, for example 400 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that, and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose."
      }
